The Vauxhall Vivaro Turbo D 3100 refers to the current generation (since 2019) Vivaro van equipped with a Turbo D (diesel) engine and a 3.1-tonne Gross Vehicle Weight (GVW). This GVW is commonly available across various trims like Edition, Dynamic, Prime, Sportive, Pro, and Elite, and with different engine outputs (1.5L 100/120PS, 2.0L 120/145/180PS). I will use data points representative of the 3100 GVW models, focusing on the 2.0L diesel engines which are frequently associated with higher GVWs.

